\", \"q\": \"Area-level demographic and socioeconomic characteristics were also correlated with deprivation level\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Addresses were used to assign cases to one of 99 Utah small statistical areas\"}]}, {\"v\": \"surveillance/descriptive\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Confirmed COVID-19 cases reported by local health departments and UDOH to the Utah National Electronic Disease Surveillance System\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Binary logistic regression was used to calculate unadjusted odds ratios (ORs) for incidence, hospitalization, and testing in each HII quintile\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Rates for four age groups (≤24, 25–44, 25–64, and ≥65 years) were weighted to a U.S. Census 2000 age-standardized population\"}, {\"loc\": \"table 2\", \"q\": \"Weighted ORs were calculated by estimating the number of persons with the outcome of interest based on the age-weighted rates for each Health Improvement Index quintile.\"}, {\"loc\": \"table 2\", \"q\": \"Confidence intervals that do not span 1.0 are considered significant\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}